-  This file was automatically generated - do not edit
+  Renders the docs header with the mark and the site title both linking to the landing
+  page, the same two controls the landing page's own header carries.
+
+  This is Material's own partials/header.html with two changes. The logo reads
+  landing_root rather than the docs root, and the title block is one link. The block
+  holds both the site name and the page title that replaces it on scroll, so wrapping
+  it leaves one tab stop and the same target whichever of the two is showing.
+
+  The homepage is derived the way the pane's Home row derives it in partials/nav.html,
+  so it follows the deployed root on the custom domain and on the project subpath. On
+  404.html base_url is a rooted path that may end in a slash, which the replace folds.
+  The theme environment has autoescape off, so every added value carries the e filter.
+
+  The installed partial and the diff to this file live in overrides/.upstream/partials.
+  After editing this file, run: uv run python tools/rederive_overrides.py --record
 -#}
